{
"content_id": "19283",
"reference_id": 18451,
"version": "1.0.4",
"title": "Jonah 1:2",
"media_type": "Text",
"index_reference": "32001002",
"language": "eng",
"review_level": "Professional",
"content": "<ul><li><p>By the time of Jonah, Nineveh already had a long history (see <a href=\"https://ref.ly/Gen10:12\">Genesis 10:12</a>). It was an important city in the Assyrian Empire until it was destroyed in 612&nbsp;BC (see <a href=\"https://ref.ly/Nah1:1-Nah3:19\">Nahum 1–3</a>). Nineveh’s ruins are across the Tigris River from the modern city of Mosul, Iraq. </p></li><li><p><em>great city</em>: See <span data-bnType=\"resourceReference\" data-resourceId=\"18466\" data-resourceType=\"TyndaleStudyNotes\">study note on Jonah 3:3</span>.</p></li></ul>",
"associations": {
"passage": [
{
"start_ref": "32001002",
"start_ref_usfm": "JON 1:2",
"end_ref": "32001002",
"end_ref_usfm": "JON 1:2"
}
],
