{
"content_id": "19291",
"reference_id": 18459,
"version": "1.0.4",
"title": "Jonah 2:4",
"media_type": "Text",
"index_reference": "32002004",
"language": "eng",
"review_level": "Professional",
"content": "<ul><li><p>As Jonah was about to drown, he called out for help, life, and God&apos;s renewed presence. It is ironic that Jonah mentioned God driving him away, as Jonah himself aimed to flee to Tarshish (<a href=\"https://ref.ly/Jonah1:3\">Jonah 1:3</a>). </p></li><li><p><em>I will look once more</em>: Jonah was either confident he would be rescued and worship again in the temple in Jerusalem, or he was calling to the Lord in his temple from the sea (compare <a href=\"https://ref.ly/Jonah2:7\">Jonah 2:7</a>).</p></li></ul>",
"associations": {
"passage": [
{
"start_ref": "32002004",
"start_ref_usfm": "JON 2:4",
"end_ref": "32002004",
"end_ref_usfm": "JON 2:4"
}
