{
"content_id": "19306",
"reference_id": 18474,
"version": "1.0.4",
"title": "Jonah 4:2",
"media_type": "Text",
"index_reference": "32004002",
"language": "eng",
"review_level": "Professional",
"content": "<ul><li><p>Jonah explains why he initially ran away from the Lord (<a href=\"https://ref.ly/Jonah1:3\">Jonah 1:3</a>): He knew the Lord would spare the wicked Ninevites if they repented. </p></li><li><p><em>I knew</em>: Jonah almost quotes <a href=\"https://ref.ly/Exod34:6-Exod34:7\">Exodus 34:6–7</a>, which is about Israel’s covenant with the Lord. Even in the Old Testament, God wanted to spread salvation to all nations (see <a href=\"https://ref.ly/Matt28:18-Matt28:20\">Matthew 28:18–20</a>).</p></li></ul>",
"associations": {
