"version": "1.0.4",
"title": "Jonah 4:6",
"media_type": "Text",
"index_reference": "32004006",
"language": "eng",
"review_level": "Professional",
"content": "<ul><li><p>LORD is the English title used in many Bible translations to represent God’s covenant name, <em>Yahweh</em>, in his relationship with Israel(see, for example, <a href=\"https://ref.ly/Ps72:18\">Psalm 72:18</a>). God did these things to show his covenant love toward Jonah and those in Israel with similar attitudes. </p></li><li><p><em>appointed</em>: see <span data-bnType=\"resourceReference\" data-resourceId=\"18449\" data-resourceType=\"TyndaleStudyNotes\">study note on Jonah 1:17</span>.</p></li></ul>",
